virglrenderer: Venus refuses a linear image with INPUT_ATTACHMENT

What: vkCreateImage's check (vkr_image_info_ok, so also the vkGetDeviceImage*
queries) and both guest-facing image format queries refuse a LINEAR image (also
the emulated LINEAR DRM modifier) with VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT unless
the format's own linear tiling has a colour or depth attachment feature, which
is what that usage needs without VK_IMAGE_CREATE_EXTENDED_USAGE_BIT. Neither Mac
driver has linear attachment features, so there every such image is refused
(VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, a "refused" line in qemu.log).
Why: KosmicKrisp makes every 2D image with INPUT_ATTACHMENT a 2D array texture,
and Metal ends the process at vkBindImageMemory2 for a linear one ("Linear
texture: must be of type MTLTextureType2D"): QEMU and the VM end. Without
EXTENDED_USAGE KosmicKrisp's format query refuses that usage (#598,
virgl-venus-linear-modifier-usage.patch). With EXTENDED_USAGE it checks no usage
against the format's features and says yes, so vkr's check, which asks the
driver, let the image through. Mesa 26.3's Zink asks that way for an X11 window
through Xwayland: on an Omarchy 4.0 VM updated to Mesa 26.3.1, `glxinfo -B` with
MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=zink ended the VM (crash report: kk_BindImageMemory2
-> mtl_new_texture_with_descriptor_linear -> _mtlValidateStrideTextureParameters).
With the query refusing it too, Zink picks an image it can have.
Upstream: KosmicKrisp's query should refuse it (its comment says linear images
cannot be input attachments); not reported. The check is vkr's, as the other
image limits are.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-image-limits.c, cases zink-extended (vkCreateImage,
plain LINEAR), zink-extended-modifier (the emulated LINEAR modifier),
zink-extended-query (both query versions refuse it), linear-extended (a plain
linear image with EXTENDED_USAGE is still made); a 4.0 VM on Mesa 26.3.1 runs
Zink on X11 without ending.
